{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OU", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ed114b8851eab6c3b79394d702d79c58b049d6f320052b48e422a41395318834", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis spectral sequence is fundamental in proving foundational results on\ncohomology of sheaves.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ff1d10f12453b010ad825096ce9c75dd67cd79681e81aec93fdeec8338942a27", "unit_id": "tag:03OU:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})\\to \\textit{PAb}(\\mathcal{C})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-forget-injectives}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c3bde646677b244425590fb9e4c1968b2c03492f1d9fa81e448df639221bbaf5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a59e1fbe3f0d4d587b634d38c852a9df34f9a03a05b58bf7ecce8e1ad6411c96", "source_text": "The forgetful functor <MATH_0001>\ntransforms injectives into injectives.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81f3f1cce421f225e1a18b155ad91b6b9c6cbb38f42545b7bb7a2f65d579772a", "unit_id": "tag:03OV:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03OU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-injective-abelian-sheaf-injective-presheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dcde977d835852eece1e7807ae70f85f817c3836ee93f80b99bb9b7c5a7fb857", "source_text": "This is formal using the fact that the forgetful functor has a left adjoint,\nnamely sheafification, which is an exact functor. For more details see\nCohomology on Sites,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ade49d58c688729370c346fddd52d14ae3753d610b68b02ea97661268c21d337", "unit_id": "tag:03OV:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nE_2^{p, q}\n=\n\\check H^p(\\mathcal{U}, \\underline{H}^q(\\mathcal{F}))\n\\Rightarrow\nH^{p+q}(U, \\mathcal{F}),\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\underline{H}^q(\\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0008": "$V \\mapsto H^q(V, \\mathcal{F})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-cech-ss}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:157fc5381e74467890aef3b3606b66f95c7f3cdceee6f7c4dc3eef7dbd62d719", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ffec5001d1b1ae0f49c85da2a211b0520e1caab40c362d7c8612dd362319c8d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. For any covering\n<MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003>\nand any abelian sheaf <MATH_0004> on <MATH_0005>\nthere is a spectral sequence\n<MATH_0006>\nwhere <MATH_0007> is the abelian presheaf\n<MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf3d67b1c5fc4cbf5d717f689c3bc6f5faf4be280ba04252ad858eb38ec03166", "unit_id": "tag:03OW:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}\\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Gamma(U, I^\\bullet) \\ar[r] &\n\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet) \\\\\n& \\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F}) \\ar[u]\n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Gamma(U, I^\\bullet) \\to\n\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^0(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}\\to \\mathcal{I}^0$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0008": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0009": "$\\textit{PAb}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0010": "$\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^0(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)\n\\to \\check{\\mathcal{C}}^1(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0013": "$H^0(U, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0014": "$q$", "MATH_0015": "$p$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\prod_{i_0, \\ldots, i_p}\nH^q(U_{i_0} \\times_U \\ldots \\times_U U_{i_p}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\prod_{i_0, \\ldots, i_p}\n\\underline{H}^q(\\mathcal{F})(U_{i_0} \\times_U \\ldots \\times_U U_{i_p})\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$E_1^{p, q}$", "MATH_0018": "$E_2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-forget-injectives}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-hom-injective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-cech-spectral-sequence}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:57c3c3d194689fe97b0db535ca168389a3090a21648ec6ca78f6c8b62f371356", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:06b49241ea5cc3e487f0383847d8aecdf54027135d92034ce19ef8b128bcb3c7", "source_text": "Choose an injective resolution <MATH_0001> in\n<MATH_0002>, and consider the double complex\n<MATH_0003>\nand the maps\n<MATH_0004>\nHere the horizontal map is the natural map\n<MATH_0005>\nto the left column, and the vertical map is induced by\n<MATH_0006> and lands in the bottom row.\nBy assumption, <MATH_0007> is a complex of injectives in\n<MATH_0008>, hence by\nLemma <REF_0001>, it is a complex of injectives in\n<MATH_0009>. Thus, the rows of the double complex are\nexact in positive degrees (Lemma <REF_0002>), and\nthe kernel of <MATH_0010>\nis equal to\n<MATH_0011>, since <MATH_0012>\nis a complex of sheaves. In particular, the cohomology of the total complex\nis the standard\ncohomology of the global sections functor <MATH_0013>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nFor the vertical direction, the <MATH_0014>th cohomology group of the <MATH_0015>th column is\n<MATH_0016>\nin the entry <MATH_0017>. So this is a standard double complex spectral\nsequence, and the <MATH_0018>-page is as prescribed. For more details see\nCohomology on Sites,\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0fd6c77b0fba69bb26464682b913eb712b4f426dca23c35b8770fcf2ade1e0e9", "unit_id": "tag:03OW:proof"}
